---
// src/pages/buy-blue-staffy-puppies-uk/index.astro — REBUILT from the approved board record
// (data/boards/buy-blue-staffy-puppies-uk.json, approved 2026-09-20). Hand-written and NOT
// regenerated by `npm run extract`: the slug is listed in data/facts/rebuilt.json, so
// `migration_parity.py` skips it and `facts_preserved_check.py`, `link_parity_check.py` and
// `verbatim_set_check.py` are its gates instead.
//
// THIS IS THE LISTING PAGE. Its question is "which one, and is it still available", so the
// six rows of data/puppies.json are the page and every count on it is the length of a
// filtered list rather than a number typed into prose. The migrated block's "Males: 2
// Females: 2 Age: 12 weeks, 6 days" is nowhere on it (`dropped.text`), and neither is the
// £850 to £1,200 band, the £300 non-refundable deposit, the five weeks' free insurance or
// the 500-reader newsletter — each logged in the record's `dropped` with its reason.
//
// THE MONEY STAYS ON /blue-staffy-pup-sale-uk/ (spec §2). One money figure is stated here —
// the £500 refundable deposit, which is the thing this page asks a reader to do — and the
// price table and the delivery table are the price page's, linked from four sections rather
// than printed a second time.
//
// THIS PAGE OWNS THE PER-PUPPY PRODUCT/OFFER MARKUP (spec §2, the record's `puppies` intent).
// One Product node per available dog, each with its own Offer, its own price out of
// data/puppies.json and a url pointing at that dog's page. NO `availability`: an InStock
// claim belongs to one dog's own page and scripts/schema_check.py blocks it anywhere else,
// which is the same line /blue-staffy-pup-sale-uk/ draws around its AggregateOffer. That
// page carries the band; this one carries the six offers; neither claims the other's.
//
// WORKING RULE 15 (faithful rewrite). The VERBATIM SET — the migrated H1, every H2/H3
// carrying a target keyword, the first paragraph under each of those headings, the FAQ
// questions and every image alt — is carried WORD FOR WORD. The carried wording is READ OFF
// THE RECORD (`sections[].heading`, `sections[].verbatim_opening`, `assets[].alt`) rather
// than retyped here, so a curly quote or a stray space cannot drift between the record the
// breeder approved and the page that ships. Fourteen deviations are recorded in the record's
// `verbatim.changed` with their reasons — including the H1: the breeder picked "One-Stop"
// over the migrated "#1-Stop", and a rank measured against nothing is not a claim this site
// makes. Everything else on the page is written fresh, in Lisa Bright's first person.
//
// WORKING RULE 16. The hero is `H-FS1` (the puppy-grid mosaic right of the copy, tick list
// under the lede) and the counter strip is `C-FS3` (a seam bar in a card beside the heading,
// labels beside the figures) — the for-sale family's own arrangements, resolved through
// `pickedStyle()` exactly as every other section's pick is, and neither of them the ones
// /blue-staffy-pup-sale-uk/ took. The counter prints the record's three sourced `stats` rows:
// the available count, the males and the females, every one of them a filter over
// data/puppies.json.
//
// THIRTEEN SECTIONS, in the record's order, each mounted in the style `approval.picks` names.
// No link, image or section is here that the board does not carry. NO EMBED: this page had
// none (data/facts/buy-blue-staffy-puppies-uk.json — embeds empty; data/page-map.json records
// 0), so working rule 14 has no id to carry and none is invented.
//
// H4-H6 ARE WRITTEN HERE, not in the record (amendment 2.1): the approved outline stops at
// the H3 the breeder read. Every ladder sentence traces to the migrated body or to a file
// under data/ (amendment 6f), and the H6 lines all open on the record's own
// `tuple.h6_prefixes` entry, "Step Note:". Every heading renders through `titleCase()`
// (amendment 4b) — approved wording, site-wide case.
import PageShell from '../../layouts/PageShell.astro';
import Hero from '../../components/kit/Hero.astro';
import CounterStrip from '../../components/kit/CounterStrip.astro';
import InfoCard from '../../components/kit/InfoCard.astro';
import PuppyCard from '../../components/kit/PuppyCard.astro';
import Testimonial from '../../components/kit/Testimonial.astro';
import ContactFormKit from '../../components/kit/ContactFormKit.astro';
import Faq from '../../components/kit/Faq.astro';
import { sectionsFromRecord } from '../../lib/sections';
import { pickedStyle } from '../../lib/pickedStyle';
import { bakedAssets } from '../../lib/assets';
import { recordText, countedFigures, ledgeText, numberWord, type LedgeEntry } from '../../lib/recordText';
import { boxClass } from '../../lib/boardStyles';
import { titleCase as T } from '../../lib/headings';
import { loadFaq } from '../../lib/faq';
import { SITE, SITE_URL, abs, type PuppyRow } from '../../lib/site';
import puppiesJson from '../../../data/puppies.json';
import reviewsJson from '../../../data/reviews.json';
import record from '../../../data/boards/buy-blue-staffy-puppies-uk.json';

const path = '/buy-blue-staffy-puppies-uk/';
// The picked meta variants and H1, BY INDEX from the approval — never retyped here.
const approvedTitle = record.meta_set.titles[record.approval!.meta!.title];
const description = record.meta_set.descriptions[record.approval!.meta!.description];
const h1 = record.h1.variants[record.approval!.h1];

// The seven photographs plus the two mosaic tiles, by slot, at their ORIGINAL public paths
// with the alt text the record baked (working rule 11; seven of those alts are seven elements
// of the verbatim set, and `listing-trust`'s is the one the record repaired — the migrated
// wording named the former city). The two tiles reuse two of the seven files at their own
// paths and carry their own alt, because a page may not render the same alt twice
// (`img-alt-present-and-unique`) and may not rename a served file (working rule 11).
// A missing slot throws at build rather than rendering an image with no alt.
const asset = bakedAssets(record);
const heroPhoto = asset('listing-hero');
const heroTile2 = asset('listing-hero-tile-2');
const heroTile3 = asset('listing-hero-tile-3');
const buyNow = asset('listing-buy-now');
const pupsNearYou = asset('listing-pups-near-you');
const trust = asset('listing-trust');
const deliveryVan = asset('listing-delivery');
const ownerLondon = asset('listing-owner-london');
const ownerCardiff = asset('listing-owner-cardiff');

// THE SIX PUPPIES, filtered on `status` rather than hard-coded: a puppy leaving the list is a
// data edit, not a page edit. All six rows are Available today. Their card links are the
// grid's own data and are exempt from link parity (amendment 6b).
const available = (puppiesJson as PuppyRow[]).filter((p) => p.status === 'Available');

// THE TITLE'S COUNT IS DERIVED. The approved title reads "…: Six Available In Carlisle", and
// "Six" is a count of the rows above, not a word the breeder chose: typed, it goes wrong the
// day a puppy is reserved while every card and counter beside it moves. So the page renders
// the approved wording with that ONE word replaced by the live count. The assert is the other
// half: the approved title must carry exactly one "<Number> Available", or there is nothing
// honest to replace and the build stops — a reworded title goes back to the board rather
// than being quietly re-counted, and a litter with nobody available cannot claim "Zero".
const COUNT_WORD = /\b(One|Two|Three|Four|Five|Six|Seven|Eight|Nine|Ten|Eleven|Twelve) Available\b/g;
const countHits = approvedTitle.match(COUNT_WORD) ?? [];
if (countHits.length !== 1) {
  throw new Error(`buy-blue-staffy-puppies-uk: the approved title "${approvedTitle}" carries `
    + `${countHits.length} "<Number> Available" phrases — exactly one is derived from data/puppies.json`);
}
if (available.length === 0) {
  throw new Error('buy-blue-staffy-puppies-uk: no puppy is Available, and the approved title states '
    + 'a count of available puppies — re-board the title before building');
}
const countWord = numberWord(available.length);
const title = approvedTitle.replace(COUNT_WORD, `${countWord.charAt(0).toUpperCase()}${countWord.slice(1)} Available`);
// "All six puppies came from the same two dogs" counts the LITTER — every row, sold or not.
const litterWord = numberWord((puppiesJson as PuppyRow[]).length);

// ONE review, given room. `approval.picks` gives this section the S3 BED and the mode is the
// record's own note ("MODE: single"), passed explicitly — the same split
// /blue-staffy-pup-sale-uk/ makes in the other direction. Rachel L. is the row
// data/reviews.json sources to THIS page, which is why she is the one this page gives its
// single slot. She is NOT exclusive to it: /blue-staffy-pup-sale-uk/ renders all three rows as
// a grid, so the rotation the record describes is about which review each page gives a slot of
// its own — three real reviews and no fourth to invent. The other two slots here are not
// opened, so no REVIEW_PLACEHOLDER is counted.
const rachel = reviewsJson.filter((r) => r.name === 'Rachel L.');
if (rachel.length !== 1) {
  throw new Error('buy-blue-staffy-puppies-uk: data/reviews.json no longer holds the Rachel L. row');
}

// THE THIRTEEN FAQ ROWS THE RECORD NAMES, BY ID, in the record's order. Twelve of them carry
// the migrated accordion's questions word for word (rule 15) and the thirteenth is this
// page's own `listing-availability`. The answers are data, not page copy: `listing-cost`
// interpolates the deposit out of data/settings.json rather than stating a figure.
const faqSection = record.sections.find((s) => s.id === 'questions')!;
const faqRows = loadFaq();
const faqs = faqSection.tree.map((n) => {
  const row = faqRows.find((r) => r.id === n.heading);
  if (!row) throw new Error(`buy-blue-staffy-puppies-uk: data/faq.json has no row ${n.heading}`);
  return row;
});

// The carried wording, read off the record rather than retyped (see the rule 15 note above).
// `heading` is the approved heading — already the repaired one where `verbatim.changed` says
// so — and `opening` is the first paragraph the section carries word for word.
// All five readers are `src/lib/recordText.ts`, shared with the why-us and the price page.
const { sec, heading, opening, node } = recordText(record);
// The delivery H3 and its paragraph are a TREE node's, not a section's: the migrated page put
// that keyword heading one level down, so the record carries the pair there — already with
// the former city excised (verbatim.changed, Known Issue 16).
const deliveryH3 = node('delivery', 0);

// EVERY FIGURE ON THIS PAGE IS COUNTED HERE, and the record's `n` is the expectation it is
// counted against — `countedFigures()` in the same module. The section below says in as many
// words that none of these figures is written by hand; mapping the record's `n` straight onto
// the strip made that sentence false, because the record's `n` IS a hand-written number — a
// true one on the day it was boarded, and the first thing to go stale when a puppy is
// reserved. So the counts come from the same filtered list the grid renders, and a count that
// no longer equals what the board approved throws at build rather than printing a figure
// nobody checked. That is the point of keeping both: the data decides what prints, and the
// record decides when a human has to look.
const COUNTED: Record<string, number> = {
  'data/puppies.json#count(status=Available)': available.length,
  'data/puppies.json#count(sex=male)': available.filter((p) => p.sex === 'male').length,
  'data/puppies.json#count(sex=female)': available.filter((p) => p.sex === 'female').length,
};
const counted = countedFigures(COUNTED, 'buy-blue-staffy-puppies-uk');

const heroSection = sec('top');
const heroChips = (heroSection.hero!.chips as LedgeEntry[]).map(ledgeText);
// THE HERO LEDGE IS COUNTED TOO. H-FS1's ledge is `ticks`, and the first of the record's three
// says "3 males and 3 females" — two figures, in a sentence, and typing them here would be the
// same defect one element further down the page. The sentence is rebuilt from the counts and
// checked against the wording the breeder approved, so a litter that changes fails the build
// instead of shipping a hero that contradicts the strip under it.
const males = COUNTED['data/puppies.json#count(sex=male)'];
const females = COUNTED['data/puppies.json#count(sex=female)'];
const heroTicks = (heroSection.hero!.ticks as LedgeEntry[]).map((t, i) => {
  const approvedText = ledgeText(t);
  if (i !== 0) return approvedText;
  const derived = `${males} males and ${females} females`;
  if (derived !== approvedText) {
    throw new Error(`buy-blue-staffy-puppies-uk: the approved hero tick reads "${approvedText}" `
      + `and data/puppies.json counts "${derived}" — the litter moved`);
  }
  return derived;
});
const heroStats = heroSection.stats!.map(counted);
const counterStats = sec('at-a-glance').stats!.map(counted);

const sections = sectionsFromRecord(record);

// Each section's approved arrangement, resolved through the same `boxClass()` the board
// preview called: what the breeder signed off is what ships.
const style = (id: string) => pickedStyle(record, id);
const box = (id: string) => boxClass(style(id));
const heroStyle = style('top');
const counterStyle = style('at-a-glance');

// "Mo-Su 09:00-23:00" as a sentence, from the setting rather than typed as prose.
const hours = SITE.hours.replace('Mo-Su ', 'from ').replace('-', ' to ');

// The record's schema plan: WebPage (BaseLayout) + one Product per available puppy + FAQPage.
// Each Product's price is that row's `price_gbp` and its url is that dog's own page, so the
// markup and the grid read the same file and can never disagree. NO `availability` anywhere:
// an InStock claim belongs to one dog's own page (scripts/schema_check.py blocks it on every
// other), and a listing claiming stock for six dogs at once would be claiming it six times
// over. The FAQPage node is built from the SAME thirteen rows the accordion renders;
// data/faq.json keeps the sentence-case wording, which is what `name` reads, and the visible
// question is cased at render (amendment 6g). No `dateModified` here on purpose — BaseLayout
// adds the WebPage node with the git-derived dates.
// The Products sit inside ONE ItemList: they are a catalogue of the litter, not the page's own
// single offer, which is what tests/render/checks/schema.ts's `inItemList` reads them as.
const pageSchema = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'ItemList',
    '@id': `${abs(path)}#available-puppies`,
    name: 'Blue Staffy puppies available now',
    numberOfItems: available.length,
    itemListElement: available.map((p, i) => ({
      '@type': 'ListItem',
      position: i + 1,
      item: {
    '@type': 'Product',
    '@id': `${abs(path)}#puppy-${p.slug}`,
    name: `${p.name} – Blue Staffy puppy`,
    description: `${p.name} is a ${p.colour.toLowerCase()} ${p.sex} Staffordshire Bull Terrier `
      + `puppy from Blue Staffy UK in ${SITE.location_label.replace(' · ', ', ')}.`,
    image: abs(`/images/puppies/${p.slug}-card-800.webp`),
    brand: { '@type': 'Brand', name: SITE.site_name },
    offers: {
      '@type': 'Offer',
      price: String(p.price_gbp),
      priceCurrency: 'GBP',
      url: abs(`/available-puppies/${p.slug}/`),
      seller: { '@id': `${SITE_URL}/#business` },
    },
      },
    })),
  },
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'FAQPage',
    '@id': `${abs(path)}#faq`,
    mainEntity: faqs.map((r) => ({
      '@type': 'Question',
      name: r.q,
      acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: r.a },
    })),
  },
];
---
<PageShell
  title={title}
  description={description}
  canonical={path}
  ogType="article"
  schema={pageSchema}
  sections={sections}
>
  {/* 01 top — hero, picked style H-FS1 (a three-tile puppy-grid mosaic right of the copy, the
      tick list under the lede). The ledge is `ticks`, so the record's chips are handed over
      and the arrangement is what decides they do not render, and there are no CTA buttons
      (amendment 6a). The first tile is the migrated page's own primaryImageOfPage at its
      original path and alt. */}
  <section slot="hero" id="top" data-section-label="The puppies we have for sale today" class={box('top')}>
    <Hero
      as="h1"
      {/* TWO WORDS, because rule 10 is measured and this arrangement is tight. At 1024 the
          mosaic leaves the copy a 316px column, the approved H1 takes five lines in it, and a
          three-word eyebrow wrapped to two — which pushed the third tick 19px past the 450px
          ceiling. The kennel's town is on the tick under it and in every section below, so the
          line the eyebrow gives up is the one the page repeats anyway. */}
      eyebrow="KC registered · Microchipped"
      title={T(h1)}
      lede="I am Lisa Bright. These are our blue Staffy puppies looking for homes."
      layout={heroStyle.layout.hero ?? 'mosaic'}
      align={heroStyle.layout.align ?? 'left'}
      media={heroStyle.layout.media ?? 'right'}
      ledge={heroStyle.layout.ledge ?? 'ticks'}
      chips={heroChips}
      ticks={heroTicks}
      stats={heroStats}
      mosaic={[
        { src: heroPhoto.file, alt: heroPhoto.alt, w: heroPhoto.w, h: heroPhoto.h,
          srcset: '/images/staffordshire-bull-terrier-for-sale-uk-ready-240.webp 240w, /images/staffordshire-bull-terrier-for-sale-uk-ready-400.webp 400w, /images/staffordshire-bull-terrier-for-sale-uk-ready-760.webp 760w' },
        { src: heroTile2.file, alt: heroTile2.alt, w: heroTile2.w, h: heroTile2.h, caption: heroTile2.caption,
          srcset: '/images/blue-staffy-pups-near-you-240.webp 240w, /images/blue-staffy-pups-near-you-400.webp 400w, /images/blue-staffy-pups-near-you-760.webp 760w' },
        { src: heroTile3.file, alt: heroTile3.alt, w: heroTile3.w, h: heroTile3.h, caption: heroTile3.caption,
          srcset: '/images/blue-staffy-puppy-delivery-uk-240.webp 240w, /images/blue-staffy-puppy-delivery-uk-400.webp 400w, /images/blue-staffy-puppy-delivery-uk-760.webp 760w' },
      ]}
    />
    <p>
      <a href="/buy-staffy-puppies-for-sale-uk/">Why families choose us, and the evidence for it</a> is
      argued at length on its own page, and this one stays out of its way.
      <a href="/blue-staffy-pup-sale-uk/">What a puppy costs and what delivery adds</a> is set out
      there as well, in two tables, so nothing here has to be worked out twice. On this page you
      pick a dog, see who their parents are, and read the three steps between a first message
      and collection day. Everything on it is here in the house with us in Carlisle: there is no
      waiting list, and nothing below is a litter that has not been born yet.
    </p>
  </section>

  {/* 02 at-a-glance — stats, picked style C-FS3 (a seam bar in a card beside the heading, each
      label beside its figure). The strip prints the record's three `stats` rows, and all three
      are filters over data/puppies.json rather than numbers typed into this page. */}
  <section id="at-a-glance" data-section-label="How many are left, and the sex split" class={box('at-a-glance')}>
    <div class="bl-head">
      <p class="bl-eyebrow">Counted from our own list</p>
      <h2>{T(heading('at-a-glance'))}</h2>
      <p class="bl-lede">
        How many puppies are still looking, and how this litter splits between the sexes. Every
        one of them is microchipped and vet checked before it leaves us, and none of these
        figures is written by hand — a reserved dog changes them the day it happens.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="bl-body">
      <CounterStrip
        stats={counterStats}
        tiles={counterStyle.layout.tiles ?? 'seam'}
        label={counterStyle.layout.label ?? 'beside'}
      />
      <p>Take a puppy off our list and the bar above moves with it, because the bar is the list.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* 03 puppies — puppies, picked style S2 (a two-up card grid beside the heading, roomier
      than the price page's three-up). The migrated H2 and its opening line are carried word
      for word. The cards are rows of data/puppies.json rendered by PuppyCard, and their own
      hrefs are grid data rather than prose the breeder wrote an anchor for. THIS SECTION IS
      WHAT THE PER-PUPPY PRODUCT NODES DESCRIBE. */}
  <section id="puppies" data-section-label="Buy blue Staffy puppies UK-wide" class={box('puppies')}>
    <div class="bl-head">
      <h2>{T(heading('puppies'))}</h2>
      <p class="bl-lede">{opening('puppies')}</p>
    </div>
    <div class="bl-body">
      <div class="bl-cards">
        {available.map((p) => <PuppyCard slug={p.slug} />)}
      </div>
      <img
        class="bl-img"
        src={buyNow.file}
        alt={buyNow.alt}
        width={buyNow.w}
        height={buyNow.h}
        srcset="/images/buy-staffordshire-bull-terrier-uk-now-760.webp 760w, /images/buy-staffordshire-bull-terrier-uk-now.webp 918w"
        sizes="(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 420px"
        loading="lazy"
        decoding="async"
      />
      <h3>{T('What Each Card Tells You')}</h3>
      <p>
        A name, whether the dog is a male or a female, the colour we would call them, the price
        for that dog and whether anybody has reserved them yet. Open a card and you get that
        puppy's own page and the rest of their photographs.
      </p>
      <h3>{T('Why The List Changes')}</h3>
      <p>
        Nobody types this grid. It is drawn from our own list of available puppies, and that
        list is updated regularly — so a dog leaves the grid the hour we mark them reserved,
        not whenever somebody next gets round to the page.
        <a href="/blue-staffy-pup-sale-uk/">The price table, and what the deposit leaves to pay</a> is
        on the page that owns both figures.
      </p>
      <h4>{T('Nothing Here Is A Placeholder')}</h4>
      <p>
        Every card is a dog we have in the house. We do not list a litter before it is born and
        we do not leave a reserved puppy up to draw enquiries.
      </p>
      <h5>{T('One Deposit Holds One Named Dog')}</h5>
      <p>We will not hold two puppies for the same household while a decision is being made.</p>
      <h6>{T('Step Note: Name the puppy in your first message')}</h6>
      <p>
        <a href="#enquiry">Tell us which one you mean</a> and we confirm that dog is still free
        before anything else is discussed.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* 04 gallery — standard, picked style S1 (prose with the photograph on the right). Restored
      under rule 15 at the migrated page's own heading and opening paragraph. The photograph
      moves here from `puppies`, which keeps its own; no new image is added, because working
      rule 11 reuses what is already served. The migrated "See Our Blue Staffy Puppies in
      Action!" block is NOT restored beside it — this page carries no video id to put under
      it, and that heading is in `verbatim.changed` as a drop. */}
  <section id="gallery" data-section-label="Blue Staffy puppy gallery" class={box('gallery')}>
    <div class="bl-head">
      <h2>{T(heading('gallery'))}</h2>
      <p class="bl-lede">{opening('gallery')}</p>
    </div>
    <div class="bl-body">
      <div class="bl-prose">
        <img
          class="bl-img"
          src={pupsNearYou.file}
          alt={pupsNearYou.alt}
          width={pupsNearYou.w}
          height={pupsNearYou.h}
          srcset="/images/blue-staffy-pups-near-you-760.webp 760w, /images/blue-staffy-pups-near-you.webp 870w"
          sizes="(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 420px"
          loading="lazy"
          decoding="async"
        />
        <div class="bl-stub">
          <p>
            They are photographed in the rooms they live in rather than against a backdrop, so
            what you see is the floor they are learning to walk on. Ask for more of any one of
            them and we will send them.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* 05 parents — standard, picked style S1 (prose with the image right; no photograph on this
      record, because the two parent photographs this site holds are on
      /blue-staffy-pup-sale-uk/ and /blue-staffy-health-uk/ and data/facts lists neither of
      them for this page). Maggie and Jones, the two DNA clearances, and the one thing a
      classified advert cannot offer: the puppies are viewable with their mother. */}
  <section id="parents" data-section-label="The mother and father of this litter" class={box('parents')}>
    <div class="bl-head">
      <h2>{T(heading('parents'))}</h2>
      <p class="bl-lede">
        All {litterWord} puppies came from the same two dogs, and both of them live here. Maggie is the
        dam and Jones is the sire, and our litters are registered with the Kennel Club.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="bl-body">
      <h3>{T('Seeing Them Together')}</h3>
      <p>
        The puppies are still with Maggie, and you are welcome to see that before you decide
        anything. It is the part of buying a puppy that cannot be photographed convincingly and
        cannot be faked at all, which is why we would rather you came and watched it than took
        our word for it.
      </p>
      {/* Renamed 2026-09-21 from "What Both Parents Are Clear Of", which failed board_gate's
          five-token shingle against /blue-staffy-health-uk/'s own "Both Parents Are Clear Of
          Two Inherited Conditions". The health page owns the DNA table and this is the passing
          mention that links to it, so the listing is the side that moves; the heading was
          written fresh at Task 17 and is in no verbatim set. Record re-approved (amendment 11). */}
      <h3>{T(node('parents', 1).heading)}</h3>
      <p>
        Both are KC-registered, and both carry clear DNA results for the two conditions this
        breed is screened against, L-2-HGA and HC-HSF4.
        <a href="/blue-staffy-health-uk/">The test results for both parents, in full</a> are on
        the health page, which owns the table rather than repeating it here.
        <a href="https://www.royalkennelclub.com/search/breeds-a-to-z/breeds/terrier/staffordshire-bull-terrier/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The registry's own page for the breed</a> sets
        out what the standard asks for, if you would rather read it away from a breeder's site.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* 06 steps — takeaways, picked style S2 (three cards across, on the steel band, which no
      other buy page spends its band on). The migrated page's six-step journey collapses into
      three, because two of the six are not decisions a buyer makes and the deposit terms the
      fourth stated are the wrong ones (`dropped.text`, `dropped.prices`). The H2 is the
      migrated wording with its colliding tail moved (verbatim.changed) and the opening
      paragraph is carried whole. */}
  <section id="steps" data-section-label="Your adoption journey" class={box('steps')}>
    <div class="bl-head">
      <p class="bl-eyebrow">Three steps, and only the third costs anything</p>
      <h2>{T(heading('steps'))}</h2>
      <p class="bl-lede">{opening('steps')}</p>
    </div>
    <div class="bl-body">
      <div class="bl-cards">
        <InfoCard
          kind="fact"
          heading={T('Step One: Tell Us Which Puppy')}
          body="Name the dog from the grid above, say where you are writing from and who is in the house. We answer within 24 to 48 business hours, and it is me answering."
        />
        <InfoCard
          kind="fact"
          heading={T('Step Two: Meet Them First')}
          body="A video call, or a visit here by appointment to see the puppy with their mother. Ask for the registration papers and the DNA results before you decide, not after."
        />
        <InfoCard
          kind="fact"
          heading={T('Step Three: Reserve And Arrange Collection')}
          body={`A £${SITE.deposit_gbp} deposit, ${SITE.deposit_refundable ? 'refundable' : 'non-refundable'}, holds that one named puppy and comes off the price. Then we fix collection in ${SITE.location_label.split(' · ')[0]} or arrange the journey to you.`}
        />
      </div>
      <img
        class="bl-img"
        src={trust.file}
        alt={trust.alt}
        width={trust.w}
        height={trust.h}
        srcset="/images/uk-blue-staffy-breeders-trust-760.webp 760w, /images/uk-blue-staffy-breeders-trust.webp 952w"
        sizes="(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 420px"
        loading="lazy"
        decoding="async"
      />
      <p>
        <a href="/uk-blue-staffy-puppy-buying-guide/">Our buying guide, and the questions to put to us</a> is
        worth reading before step one, and it is written for buying from anybody rather than
        from us in particular.
        <a href="/blue-staffy-uk-breeders/">Who we are, and where the litter is raised</a> answers
        most of the rest of what a first message asks.
      </p>
      <h4>{T('You Can Stop At Any Of The Three')}</h4>
      <p>
        Nothing is owed until the deposit, and the deposit comes after you have met the puppy.
        A reader who decides the breed is wrong for them has cost us nothing at all.
      </p>
      <h5>{T('The Reply Window Is The Same For Everybody')}</h5>
      <p>Twenty-four to forty-eight business hours, whether the message is two lines or twenty.</p>
      <h6>{T('Step Note: A deposit holds a dog, not a place in a queue')}</h6>
      <p>It takes that puppy off the grid above while the rest is settled.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* 07 whats-included — standard, picked style S1 (prose with the image right; no photograph
      on this record, so the prose runs alone). The migrated heading and its opening paragraph
      are carried word for word. It is the CONTENTS and not the price: the migrated block's
      free-insurance line and its health guarantee are not restated (`dropped.prices`,
      `dropped.creds` — data/settings.json holds guarantee_days null). */}
  <section id="whats-included" data-section-label="What your puppy comes with" class={box('whats-included')}>
    <div class="bl-head">
      <h2>{T(heading('whats-included'))}</h2>
      <p class="bl-lede">{opening('whats-included')}</p>
    </div>
    <div class="bl-body">
      <p>
        The first vaccinations, the worming, the microchip, a full veterinary health check and
        the paperwork that records all four. Each is dated on the sheet, so the next person to
        treat the puppy knows exactly what has already been done and when. We state no health
        guarantee, because we have not confirmed a term for one.
        <a href="/blue-staffy-pup-sale-uk/">What a puppy costs, and what the deposit holds</a> is
        the other half of this, on the price page.
      </p>
      <h3>{T('Why The List Is Written Down')}</h3>
      <p>
        A puppy leaves with a record rather than an assurance. If a breeder cannot hand you
        the dates on paper, there is nothing for your own vet to read and nothing for you to
        check a year later.
      </p>
      <h4>{T('The List Stops Where The Paperwork Does')}</h4>
      <p>
        Five items, then the list stops. We do not invoice for any of them afterwards and we
        have not padded the list to make a puppy sound better equipped.
      </p>
      <h5>{T('Nothing Here Is Promised That Is Not Written Down')}</h5>
      <p>No term is stated for a guarantee, because we have not confirmed one.</p>
      <h6>{T('Step Note: Ask for the paperwork before you pay')}</h6>
      <p>We would rather you asked than assumed, and the answer is the same either way.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* 08 why-choose — standard, picked style S1 (prose with the image right; no photograph, so
      the section stays short). Restored under rule 15: the opening paragraph is the migrated
      one, and only the heading moved, because the migrated wording collides with a live
      heading on /blue-staffy-pup-sale-uk/ and board_gate.py fails both — the collision is
      mutual and both records changed theirs (verbatim.changed). Three sentences, and then the
      reader is sent to the page that argues it. */}
  <section id="why-choose" data-section-label="Why buy from BlueStaffyUK" class={box('why-choose')}>
    <div class="bl-head">
      <h2>{T(heading('why-choose'))}</h2>
      <p class="bl-lede">{opening('why-choose')}</p>
    </div>
    <div class="bl-body">
      <p>
        We breed from two dogs we live with, both DNA tested clear, and we register the litters
        rather than asking anybody to take our word for the lines. The puppies are raised in the
        kitchen, where a dog learns that a doorbell and a hoover are ordinary. And nobody is
        asked for money before meeting the dog they are buying.
        <a href="/buy-staffy-puppies-for-sale-uk/">The full case, reason by reason</a> belongs to
        the why-us page, and a listing that made the case twice would be selling rather than
        listing.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* 09 delivery — standard, picked style S2 (the photograph full width above two columns, at
      a tighter rhythm than the section above it). The H2 and the H3 under it are migrated
      keyword headings carried word for word, and the H3's paragraph is the migrated one with
      the former city excised and nothing else touched (verbatim.changed, Known Issue 16).
      PROSE AND NO TABLE: /blue-staffy-pup-sale-uk/ carries the two-row delivery table and a
      second copy here is the duplication the dup gate is for. No town is priced and no
      delivery window is promised. */}
  <section id="delivery" data-section-label="Staffy puppy delivery" class={box('delivery')}>
    <div class="bl-head">
      <h2>{T(heading('delivery'))}</h2>
      <p class="bl-lede">
        Collect from us, or let us arrange the journey. Which of the two costs what is on the
        price page.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="bl-body">
      <img
        class="bl-img"
        src={deliveryVan.file}
        alt={deliveryVan.alt}
        width={deliveryVan.w}
        height={deliveryVan.h}
        srcset="/images/blue-staffy-puppy-delivery-uk-760.webp 760w, /images/blue-staffy-puppy-delivery-uk.webp 1024w"
        sizes="(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 420px"
        loading="lazy"
        decoding="async"
      />
      <h3>{T(deliveryH3.heading)}</h3>
      <p>{deliveryH3.verbatim_opening}</p>
      <p>
        <a href="/blue-staffy-pup-sale-uk/">What collection and delivery cost, side by side</a> is
        the table on the price page, and it is the only place either figure is written.
        <a href="https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a819d3bed915d74e623335d/pb10308-dogs-cats-welfare-060215.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The government's welfare rules for animals in transport</a> is
        the standard the carriers we use work to.
      </p>
      <h3>{T('Coming To Collect')}</h3>
      <p>
        Allow an hour. You meet the litter, you meet Maggie, and you leave with the paperwork
        rather than waiting for it in the post. Bring a crate and somebody to sit with the
        puppy on the way home.
      </p>
      <h3>{T('If We Bring Them To You')}</h3>
      <p>
        A DEFRA-approved pet transport service carries the puppy, with their water, blanket and
        papers in the crate beside them. We tell you the day before and again when they set
        off.
      </p>
      <h3>{T('The First Night')}</h3>
      <p>
        Have the crate made up before they arrive and keep the evening quiet.
        <a href="/blue-staffy-blog-guides/">Our guides on the first weeks at home</a> cover the
        rest, and
        <a href="https://www.rspca.org.uk/adviceandwelfare/pets/dogs/health/puppycare" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">the RSPCA on caring for a puppy in its first weeks</a> is
        an opinion that is not ours.
      </p>
      <h4>{T('Distance Is The Only Thing That Moves It')}</h4>
      <p>
        Not the puppy, not the sex and not the day of the week. We work the figure out from your
        address and quote it before anything is agreed.
      </p>
      <h5>{T('No Town On This Page Is Priced')}</h5>
      <p>Our files hold a band and no per-mile rate, so a list of towns would be a guess.</p>
      <h6>{T('Step Note: Say where you are in the first message')}</h6>
      <p>A town is all we need to work your journey out.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* 10 owners — reviews, picked style S3 as the BED, with the record's own MODE: single
      passed explicitly — the same split /blue-staffy-pup-sale-uk/ makes. Rachel L. is the one
      of the three real reviews that speaks to the process a reader of this page is about to
      start, and she is the row data/reviews.json sources to this page. The two migrated
      testimonials, Becky W. and Daniel H., are in `dropped.names`: neither appears in any file
      on disk, and the quotation beside the second photograph is not carried. Both photographs
      are, at their original paths and alt text. */}
  <section id="owners" data-section-label="Why UK families trust BlueStaffyUK" class={box('owners')}>
    <div class="bl-head">
      <h2>{T(heading('owners'))}</h2>
      <p class="bl-lede">{opening('owners')}</p>
    </div>
    <div class="bl-body">
      <Testimonial mode="single" reviews={rachel} />
      <div class="bl-prose">
        <img
          class="bl-img"
          src={ownerLondon.file}
          alt={ownerLondon.alt}
          width={ownerLondon.w}
          height={ownerLondon.h}
          loading="lazy"
          decoding="async"
        />
        <img
          class="bl-img"
          src={ownerCardiff.file}
          alt={ownerCardiff.alt}
          width={ownerCardiff.w}
          height={ownerCardiff.h}
          loading="lazy"
          decoding="async"
        />
      </div>
      <p>
        One review, because one is what this page is sourced for. The other two families wrote
        about pages of their own, and they are quoted there rather than here.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* 11 questions — faq, picked style S1 (the accordion under its heading). Thirteen rows of
      data/faq.json: twelve carry the migrated accordion's questions word for word, because
      they are elements of this page's verbatim set and not the outline's to reword, and the
      thirteenth is this page's own row about the list going out of date. Seven of the twelve
      are breed and behaviour questions this page does not own: each is answered in a sentence
      and its row is SOURCED to the page that evidences it. */}
  <section id="questions" data-section-label="FAQs for buyers" class={box('questions')}>
    <div class="bl-head">
      <h2>{T(heading('questions'))}</h2>
      <p class="bl-lede">{opening('questions')}</p>
    </div>
    <div class="bl-body">
      <p>
        Thirteen rows, in the order they arrive in our inbox. The first is the one this page
        exists to answer — whether the dog you are looking at is still free — and the rest are
        the questions the old version of this page was asked, kept in the words they were asked
        in. Where an answer belongs to the breed rather than to this litter, it is one sentence
        and a link to the page that evidences it.
      </p>
      <Faq items={faqs} />
      <h4>{T('No Answer Here Sets A Price Of Its Own')}</h4>
      <p>
        The one that mentions the deposit gives the same figure as the cards and the steps
        above.
      </p>
      <h5>{T('Ask Us The One That Is Not Here')}</h5>
      <p>Thirteen rows cannot cover a litter. Put the fourteenth to us and we will answer it.</p>
      <h6>{T('Step Note: A question is not a commitment')}</h6>
      <p>Nobody is put on a list for asking one.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* 12 enquiry — form, picked style S3 (the form in a card with the heading beside it). The
      one enquiry form on this page, and it is here because this is the listing: a reader who
      has just read six cards should be able to name one without navigating. The migrated
      heading was a form widget's label repeated on five pages and is in `verbatim.changed`;
      its opening paragraph is carried, minus the 24-hour promise this site does not make.
      ContactFormKit renders its own note and the privacy link. */}
  <section id="enquiry" data-section-label="Ask about a particular puppy" class={box('enquiry')}>
    <div class="bl-head">
      <h2>{T(heading('enquiry'))}</h2>
      <p class="bl-lede">{opening('enquiry')}</p>
    </div>
    <div class="bl-body">
      <p>
        A message we can answer properly names a dog from the grid, says roughly where in the
        country it is coming from, and says who lives in the house — children, other dogs,
        somebody at home in the day. Given that, the first reply can confirm the puppy is free,
        offer you a call or a time to visit, and say what follows, instead of asking it all back
        and costing you another day.
      </p>
      <ContactFormKit />
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* 13 talk-to-us — standard, picked style S2 (two columns, with brass as a hairline under
      the heading rather than as a fill). The close, and the calmest thing a listing can say:
      nothing has to be decided from a photograph. No countdown and no scarcity — the migrated
      meta title's "Before They're Gone" is in `dropped.creds`, because our own buying guide
      tells a reader to treat sales pressure as a warning sign. */}
  <section id="talk-to-us" data-section-label="Before you send anything, come and look" class={box('talk-to-us')}>
    <div class="bl-head">
      <h2>{T(heading('talk-to-us'))}</h2>
      <p class="bl-lede">
        Nothing on this page has to be decided from a photograph. Write to {SITE.email} if you
        would rather not use a form; messages are read every day, {hours}.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="bl-body">
      <h3>{T('Arranging A Time To Visit Us')}</h3>
      <p>
        The puppies live in our house, and a house has no reception desk and no viewing hours.
        Agree a time with us and somebody will be in, the litter will be awake, and you will not
        be shown round between other people's appointments.
        <a href="/uk-blue-staffy-breeders-contact/">Write to us about a particular puppy</a> if
        you would rather begin on the contact page.
      </p>
      <h3>{T('If You Are Not Sure Yet')}</h3>
      <p>
        Then the breed guide is the honest place to start, and not this page.
        <a href="/uk-staffordshire-bull-terrier-guide/">Our guide to living with the breed</a> is
        written for somebody deciding whether to have one at all, and
        <a href="https://www.pdsa.org.uk/pet-help-and-advice/looking-after-your-pet/puppies-dogs/medium-dogs/staffordshire-bull-terrier" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">the PDSA's veterinary page for the breed</a> covers
        the same ground from a vet rather than from a breeder.
      </p>
      <h4>{T('Everything Here Starts In Writing')}</h4>
      <p>
        There is no number on this site to ring, so a first message is an email or the form
        above, and the reply comes within 24 to 48 business hours.
      </p>
      <h5>{T('A Dog That Suits The House Is Worth More Than A Deposit')}</h5>
      <p>We would rather talk somebody out of a puppy than sell them the wrong one.</p>
      <h6>{T('Step Note: Come and meet them before you reserve')}</h6>
      <p>The deposit comes after the visit, never before it.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</PageShell>
